# Line-ending policy.
#
# This is not cosmetic. cmd.exe mis-parses batch files that use bare LF line
# endings: it counts double quotes and consumes following lines while looking
# for a closer, so REM comments get executed as commands and real statements
# (setlocal, set, if) are silently swallowed. The symptom here was a launcher
# that reported "[open_panel] opening !URL!" and then tried to open a FILE
# named !URL!, leaving the panel never started at all.
#
# The .bat/.cmd files in this repository are stored with LF (git's default),
# so whether the launcher worked depended on the cloner's core.autocrlf - and
# with core.autocrlf=false (common on Windows dev boxes and CI) it did not.
# Pinning eol here makes the checkout correct regardless of local config.
#
# _audit/check_batch_quotes.py enforces both invariants.

*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Shell scripts run on the Debian VM and MUST stay LF - a CRLF shebang fails
# with "bad interpreter: No such file or directory".
*.sh text eol=lf

# These are generated/compared byte-for-byte; never rewrite them.
*.db binary
*.png binary
